## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
AMD is fab-lite, relying on foundries like TSMC, exposing it to foundry capacity constraints. Its customer concentration in data centers (e.g., AI and cloud) makes it vulnerable to capex cycles. While its GPU and CPU leadership provides a moat, foundry dependency and cyclical end-markets pose medium-term risks.  

